<title>USA: Oakley Inc Q3 net income rises.</title>
<headline>Oakley Inc Q3 net income rises.</headline>
<dateline>IRVINE, Calif. 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>3 Mos ended 9/30     9 Mos ended 9/30</p>
<p>				 1996	1995(a)	1996  1995(a)</p>
<p> Net sales		 $67,785     $47,499  $179,255 $129,800</p>
<p> Cost of goods sold     20,080	14,140    52,831   37,091</p>
<p>  Gross profit	    47,705	33,359   126,424   92,709</p>
<p>Operating expenses:</p>
<p>  R&amp;D			  1,374	   928     3,335    2,435</p>
<p>  Selling		   14,482	10,437    37,039   26,533</p>
<p>  Shipping &amp; warehousing 1,820	 1,388     4,780    3,506</p>
<p>  General and admin	4,908	 3,490    12,947    9,241</p>
<p>   Total oper expenses  22,584	16,243    58,101   41,715</p>
<p> Operating income	 25,121	17,116    68,323   50,994</p>
<p> Net income		 15,653	10,231    42,364   30,393</p>
<p> Earnings per share(b)    0.22	  0.15	0.59     0.46</p>
<p> Wgtd avg shrs(b)	 71,946	68,636    71,925   66,094</p>
<p>		     (in thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: (a) Amounts reflect pro forma adjustments made by in connection with IPO for the elimination of officers' bonuses, elimination of depreciation expense on company aircraft, and tax adjustments.</p>
<p>(b) Adjusted for September stock two-for-one stock split.  </p>
<p> Other Operating Data:     (dollars in thousands)</p>
<p>			    3 Mos ended 9/30     9 Mos ended 9/30</p>
<p>				1996     1995	1996	   1995</p>
<p>Sunglasses:</p>
<p>  Units		1,381,761  911,870  3,647,270 2,643,987(a)</p>
<p>Sales before discounts(b)</p>
<p>			   $69,005  $42,599   $180,271  $120,179(a)</p>
<p>Net sales:</p>
<p>  Domestic		47,442   32,864    119,800	 89,911</p>
<p>  International	 20,343   14,635     59,455	 39,889</p>
<p>  Backlog			--	 --  19,300(c)	15,600</p>
<p>(a) Reflects a decrease of 48,858 in units and $2,150,000 in sales as a result of an increase in the returns allowance in the second quarter of 1995 for the estimated costs associated with the repurchase of diverted product from two discount retail chains.</p>
<p>(b) Does not reflect certain returns relating to defective product.</p>
<p>(c) Adjusted for all order revisions received by the company from Sunglass Hut, its largest customer, through October 16, 1996.</p>
